The current is_prime() function checks every possible divisor from 2 to n - 1. This is correct, but it can be slow for large numbers.



🚀 Possible Improvement: Make Prime Checking Faster

The loop can check only up to the square root of the number:

for i in range(2, int(n ** 0.5) + 1):

Why does this work? If a number has a factor larger than its square root, it must also have a matching factor smaller than its square root. Therefore, checking beyond the square root is unnecessary.

Another improvement would be to display the number of primes found:

print(f"Total primes found: {len(result)}")

These are optional improvements and are not part of my current implementation.



